  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5481",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have a complex relationship with M059J, as it is involved in multiple target pathways that ultimately lead to the activation of M059J. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a target for A704, which in turn is a target of palmarumycin CP18 and 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which both target M059J. This indicates a chain of molecular interactions where Mollicellin N serves as a starting point, with downstream targets that ultimately engage M059J through various biochemical mechanisms. The overlapping pathways highlight a potential role for Mollicellin N in modulating the activity of these downstream molecules, which may contribute to the broader biological effects observed in the context of M059J. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of Mollicellin N in the regulatory network that connects it to M059J, suggesting a possible functional link that warrants further investigation.",
